  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `FirstTraverseUnderTable` now gives the clearance plane and the limit in the frame where the user sets the clearance height. `in_user_frame` (`crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs`) adds `origin.z` to `height_mm` and `limit_mm`, as #2991 does for `FirstTraverseLow`.\n- The text (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`) gives the two values in mm \"measured along the tilted tool axis\". It does not call them Z values.\n- The refusal decision does not change. `table_read` and the #3081 law are the same. The shift occurs after the verdict.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3148-under-table-user-frame.md` (no `tilted` field, no stamp bump).\n\n## Readings\n\nThe case of the issue (origin Z 20, clearance 170, B 120, X +-400):\n\n- Before: \"to the clearance plane at Z150.000 ... lower the clearance plane to Z113.590 or under it\".\n- After: \"to the clearance plane at 170.000 mm ... lower the clearance plane to 133.590 mm or under it (both measured along the tilted tool axis)\".\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `first_traverse_table::a_head_tilt_past_90_under_the_table_is_refused_with_lower`. It asserts 170 and 133.590 in the user frame, the new text, no \"raise\", no Z value, `blocks_post`, and that the post does not go out.\n  - Red on the old code: `the clearance the user set: 150`.\n  - Green on the fix.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 120 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run --base origin/main` lists 241 app heavy steps. They are left to the cut gate. The change is in message text and in the two numbers of one warning. It does not change a verdict or posted G-code.\n- A cache saved before this change keeps its local numbers until the operation generates again.\n- `first_traverse.rs` was 427 lines on main before this change (over the 400-line law). This PR adds 5 lines and does not split it.\n\nChangelog: The 3+2 refusal for a first traverse that can go under the machine table now gives the clearance plane and the limit in the values that the user typed, measured along the tilted tool axis, not as local Z values.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3148\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n## Heavy lanes run on the final head (c2d5e2330)\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main` with `--only` for the 16 reached steps whose names contain multiaxis, rotary, first_traverse, tilt, verify or wcs, plus the heavy build: 17 steps, 0 failed, 25.7 min (CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1, CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=18).\n\n- Steps that ran ignored tests: `motion heavy: rotary_adaptive` (3 passed), `app heavy: rotary_field_parity` (6 passed), `app heavy: verify` (2 passed).\n- The other 13 steps hold no `#[ignore]`d test, so they ran 0 tests in this lane. They are not proof.\n- Not run: the other 224 planned heavy steps (the full \"every target\" reach). The next release gate runs them.\n",
